# Design direction

All UI work in this project must support a premium agency-style visual language.

## Design goals

- Clean, high-end, modern look
- Confident typography
- Strong spacing rhythm
- Refined motion, not excessive motion
- Premium hover states and transitions
- Balanced composition
- Clear section hierarchy
- Visually intentional layouts, not generic blocks

## Reference style

- Poppr-inspired feel
- Elegant motion
- Minimal but strong visual identity
- Premium digital agency presentation
- Modern healthcare/technology credibility for small and medium medical businesses

## When building or refining sections

- Prioritize visual polish and alignment
- Keep card layouts consistent unless asymmetry is intentionally designed
- Use subtle depth, transparency, gradients, or glass effects only when they improve the premium look
- Avoid clutter, heavy borders, random colors, or noisy UI patterns
- Maintain consistency across Services, About, Contact, FAQ, Case Studies, and Home

## Typography

- Preserve strong heading hierarchy
- Use serif or italic emphasis only when intentional and brand-appropriate
- Avoid overusing decorative styling

## Motion

- Animations should feel smooth, intentional, and professional
- Avoid gimmicky motion
- Ensure motion supports content and layout rather than distracting from it
- For layout composition, 3D / canvas layers, and immersive motion quality, follow `premium-layout-3d-motion.mdc`

## Responsive quality

Responsive quality is part of the design quality.

A section is not considered finished unless it looks intentional and balanced across mobile, tablet, laptop, desktop, and large desktop widths. Follow `responsive-mobile-first.mdc` for breakpoints and workflow.
